],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#mysql-or-mariadb","content":"Most resources for FiveM were designed to be used with MySQL 5.7 and may hit compatibility issues when using MySQL 8, i.e."},"370":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-15","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#mysql-or-mariadb","content":"More reserved keywords, like 'stored' and 'group'."},"371":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-16","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#mysql-or-mariadb","content":"Longtext / JSON fields do not support default values."},"372":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-17","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#mysql-or-mariadb","content":"MariaDB is highly recommended for compatibility, and improved performance (over all versions of MySQL)."},"373":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-18","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#should-i-use-xampp","content":"**No.** XAMPP is a *webserver stack* intended to be used for development, allowing easy local development and testing.\\\nDo not setup XAMPP just to run your database, and install MariaDB directly instead."},"374":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-19","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#configure-your-server-step","content":"Open your server configuration file."},"375":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-20","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#configure-your-server-step","content":"Add `start oxmysql` to the top of your resource list."},"376":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-21","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#configure-your-server-step","content":"Configure your mysql connection string and set it before starting any resources."},"377":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-22","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#configure-your-server-step","content":"Certain special characters are reserved or unsupported depending on your connection string.\\\nAvoid using these characters `; , / ? : @ & = + $ #`, and try swapping connection string format."},"378":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-23","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#slow-query-warnings-step","content":"You will receive warnings if a query took a long time to complete, configurable with a convar."},"379":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-24","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#slow-query-warnings-step","content":"Query time may not be entirely accurate."},"380":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-25","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#slow-query-warnings-step","content":"Slow queries may not indicate a database issue (e.g. server hitches)."},"381":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-26","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#slow-query-warnings-step","content":"Slow queries on server startup are not necessarily problematic."},"382":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-27","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#debug-step","content":"Enabling the debug option will print all queries in the server console; you can also use an array to only print from a list of resources instead."},"383":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-28","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#debug-step","content":"You can temporarily modify the resource list with commands."},"384":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-29","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#compatibility","content":"You can delete the following resources and allow oxmysql to provide their functionality."},"385":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-30","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#compatibility","content":"mysql-async"},"386":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-31","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#compatibility","content":"ghmattimysql"},"387":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-32","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#usage","content":"Resources can import oxmysql methods by including our library, granting some type-checking and minor performance improvements over raw export calls."},"388":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-33","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#lua","content":"Modify `fxmanifest.lua` for your resource, and add the following above any other script files."},"389":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-34","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#javascript","content":"You can use raw exports, or install our npm package for intellisense and similar usage as Lua."},"390":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-35","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#javascript","content":"Import the oxmysql object into your resource."},"391":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-36","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#upserting","content":"When uncertain if a row should be inserted into the database, or an existing row should be updated, queries should check for duplicate keys."},"392":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql-37","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql#upserting","content":"This is preferred over checking the existence of a row, then inserting or updating depending on the result.\\\nFurthermore, unlike using 'REPLACE INTO', the row is not deleted and re-inserted."},"393":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","type":"page","content":"Placeholders","breadcrumbs":["Docs","OxMySQL"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders"},"394":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders-0","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","content":"Placeholders allow for query parameters to be safely executed, preventing common SQL injection methods."},"395":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders-1","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","content":"Parameters can be passed an an array or object (referred to as named parameters)."},"396":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders-2","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/placeholders","content":"These are distinct from prepared statements which are handled by the MySQL server; you can use `MySQL.prepare` for more optimised and secure queries."},"397":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","type":"page","content":"Using the Debug UI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","OxMySQL"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui"},"398":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui-0","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui#main-page","content":"Main page"},"399":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui-1","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui#resource-page","content":"Resource page"},"400":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui-2","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","content":"The debug UI lets you easily see all the queries that have been executed by resources, query response times, and per-resource statistics.\nYou should only enable this during development, or with a small player count - for larger servers, look into builtin MySQL logging."},"401":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui-3","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","content":"Before using the UI first you have to make sure you have the `mysql_ui` convar set to true:"},"402":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui-4","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","content":"Also make sure that you have `command` or `command.mysql` ace permission access, then you should be able to use the `mysql` command in game."},"403":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui-5","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","content":"You *do not* need to have the `mysql_debug` enabled to use the debug ui."},"404":{"id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui-6","page_id":"/docs/oxmysql/ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/oxmysql/ui#main